ts. Browser acceptance follows the real API through revision, confirmation, LangGraph execution and trace.\n- Consume the narrowly scoped GOWM owner repair for Temporary Skill terminal device attribution and binding-derived auxiliary-link uniqueness. Consumer startup remains read-only.\n- Candidate evolution uses the existing planner and LangGraph with exact recorded Tool IO, strict policy/input/output/error checks and persisted correction feedback. PostgreSQL atomically commits the version, validation receipt, correction, pointer and outbox with CAS and idempotent retries. Candidate validation has no live Tool transport or formal writer.\n\nRestricted profiles remain deferred. Unsupported remote/provider evidence, LLM/child/subworkflow/human-confirmation recordings, missing physical inspection capability and missing authoritative trajectory timing are explicitly open; this PR does not claim full project acceptance. Field operations and deployment: NOT_RUN.\n\nValidation: final `pnpm verify:isolated -- --frozen` passes all 30 stages: 2,683 unit / 553 contract / 272 integration / 77 E2E, fresh install and cleanup exit 0. Exact committed runtime and baseline files match frozen input d7b0a6d9… / baseline 77107c3b… (2,888 checked files). Same-source restricted GOWM: 8 steps / 2 formal flows / 32 native scenarios; browser editing, invalid-JSON rejection, V2 confirmation and actual LangGraph execution pass. Owner PR23 is merged with actual merged-head CI passing.\n\nEvidence: `reports/functional-closure/FINAL_CLOSEOUT.md` and `final/VALIDATION.json`, including original raw logs and failed attempts. Official HTTP/JSON MUST protocol harness: 74 pass / 161 skip; owner verify retains 33 existing opt-in skips. These skips are explicitly not feature acceptance. No SDAR migration or runtime dependency is added.\n","created_at":"2026-10-11T17:03:09Z","updated_at":"2026-10-11T17:08:23Z","closed_at":"2026-10-11T17:08:06Z","merged_at":"2026-10-11T17:08:06Z","merge_commit_sha":"272be